## Architecture at a Glance

This project uses **DDD + Clean Architecture + CQRS**.

```
Presentation  ←  HTTP / gRPC / Message Handlers
    ↓
Application   ←  Commands, Queries, Handlers (MediatR)
    ↓
Domain        ←  Aggregates, Value Objects, Domain Events, Repository Interfaces
    ↓
Infrastructure ← Persistence (EF Core), Messaging, External Clients
```

**Layer rules:**
- Domain has zero external dependencies.
- Application references Domain only.
- Infrastructure references Application + Domain.
- Presentation references Application + Infrastructure.
- Cross-layer shortcuts are forbidden.

{{#if project.archetype}}
## Archetype: {{project.archetype}}

{{#eq project.archetype "api"}}
- This is a standard REST API with persistence.
- Domain Aggregates + EF Core repositories are required.
- No direct database access outside Infrastructure.
{{/eq}}
{{#eq project.archetype "bff-api"}}
- This is a Backend-for-Frontend. No database, no persistence layer.
- Infrastructure contains only HTTP clients and message broker adapters.
- Aggregates are not permitted — use lightweight request/response models.
{{/eq}}
{{#eq project.archetype "microservice"}}
- This is a message-driven microservice.
- Primary interface is events and commands via a message broker.
- HTTP endpoints are supplementary only.
- Domain Aggregates and Integration Events are required.
{{/eq}}
{{/if}}

## Shared Contracts

The `{{project.workspaceNamespace}}.Contracts` project is the shared integration contract library.
All inter-service DTOs and integration events live there.
No service may reference another service's internal Domain or Application layers.

## What Kiro Must Never Do

- Rename layers or change the folder structure without an approved architecture proposal.
- Add NuGet packages not listed in the approved tech stack.
- Write business logic in the Presentation layer.
- Bypass the repository pattern with direct DbContext calls in Application.
- Delete or modify `openspec/` files outside the `openspec/changes/` flow.
- Create or write files under `.kiro/specs/` — all specification outputs must go to `openspec/changes/`.
